# One of the three graphics-mode demos, ported from the assembly examples
# repository. It takes the screen off the machine, draws, waits for a key,
# then hands text mode back and returns to BASIC.
#
# The drawn screen is not text, so there is nothing sensible to read off it
# with a text dump. What is asserted is the part that can go wrong: the demo
# runs to the end, puts text mode back, and BASIC's prompt returns.

console video
timeout 60s
cycles 8000000
send \r

screen ^OK\s*$
